1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
I can’t tell my family what I want without feeling
ungrateful.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:09,300
Think it through privately, correct the reflection, then
choose whether to explore peers.

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:13,800
Planned AI organizes themes; peer stories are optional.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,300
Prepared preview. No model.

5
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:20,600
A local example offers a possibility, not an answer.

6
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:23,200
Arjun says, Not quite.

7
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:27,605
He changes the words: it is his parents, and he wants time.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,400
Now the editable reflection changes with what he said.

9
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:35,750
He wants time to decide, without advice to stay or leave.

10
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:41,795
Planned Muse Spark may organize themes to review, never
decide what is true.

11
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,300
He confirms the corrected words and keeps a private next
step.

12
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:50,300
Arjun chooses: I can ask for time before deciding.

13
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:54,370
Arjun chooses to keep the takeaway in this preview session.

14
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,780
Day four: a fictional peer names family pressure.

15
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:02,365
Another peer asks what feels hardest today.

16
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,300
Day nine.

17
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:08,160
The host can listen, but cannot decide for Arjun.

18
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:13,700
The host sets a boundary: nobody directs a relationship
choice.

19
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:17,675
Day sixteen: Dev's question remains unanswered.

20
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,165
No reply is promised; silence can remain unresolved.

21
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:27,425
Ravi's prepared route is group only, not private messaging.

22
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:31,510
His edited question appears in the preview.

23
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,130
Nothing is sent from this prepared preview.

24
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,110
No provider is verified or bookable here.

25
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,655
There are no bookings or provider matches in this preview.

26
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:48,460
Back with peers, he keeps time to decide privately.

27
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,110
Maybe later keeps that choice open.

28
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:56,875
Private reflection stays out of the group draft.

29
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,360
Arjun chooses one bounded thing that helped.

30
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:06,280
He writes about asking for time before replying.

31
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,150
Maybe later keeps sharing optional.

32
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:15,195
His private reflection can stay out of any group draft.

33
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,300
Consent remains unchecked, and posting stays disabled.

34
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:22,280
Nothing is sent.

35
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,855
His takeaway and optional draft sit side by side.

36
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:33,230
One helpful thing, if he chooses to share it later.

37
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,945
His private takeaway remains separate.

38
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:42,370
Ravi's edited question stays group only and unsent.

39
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,685
Private reflection is still private.

40
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:50,835
The Dev draft remains optional and unsent.

41
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,980
Nothing is sent.
